 size:"The central space: about 48 m long and 13.5 m wide / 157 ft by 44 ft. About half the length of a football field.",
 intro:"This is one of the best-preserved early Christian basilicas in Rome. The basilica form — a rectangular building type borrowed from Roman civic architecture — has a tall central space raised high above lower side spaces, separated by rows of columns. The upper walls are pierced with large windows called the clerestory. Look at the exterior and the interior. How does the structure of the building create such a bright, open feeling inside what looks like a plain brick shell from outside?",
