var LM01={id:"LM-01",kind:"Architecture",wide:true,title:"A Square of Miracles",object:"Pisa Cathedral and its bell tower",playable:true,
 crumb:"Late Medieval Period, circa 900 C.E. – 1400 C.E.",
 work:"Pisa Cathedral and the Leaning Tower",date:"cathedral begun 1064 C.E., bell tower begun 1173 C.E.",location:"Piazza del Duomo, Pisa, Italy",artist:"Buscheto, Rainaldo and later builders",
 headline:"Look closely at the buildings",
 alt:"A large cathedral of grey and white striped marble seen from a corner across a green lawn under a blue sky. Its tall front, on the left, rises in stepped rows of small arches topped by a triangular gable, with dark green doors at the bottom. A dome wrapped in scaffolding rises behind the roof. At the right edge, a round white tower made of stacked rows of arches leans to one side.",
 enlarge:"Enlarge image",
 image:"public/images/artworks/Pisa-Cathedral-Tower.jpg",
 imageNote:"",
 detail:{image:"public/images/artworks/Pisa-Cathedral-Interior.jpg",flex:56,alt:"The long central hall inside the cathedral, seen from the entrance. Two rows of tall columns carry rounded arches built of alternating light and dark stone. High above, a flat gold ceiling is divided into square panels. At the far end, a half-round wall glows gold with a seated figure.",caption:"Technique detail: inside, arches and walls alternate bands of light and dark stone",credit:{word:"Detail photo (interior)",url:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisa_Cathedral_Interior.jpg",author:"Eric Kilby",license:"CC BY-SA 2.0",licenseUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/",changes:"Resized from the original."}},
 detail2:{image:"public/images/artworks/Pisa-Cathedral-from-Above.jpg",flex:44,alt:"A view down from the top of the tower onto the cathedral. Its grey roofs meet in the shape of a cross, with a long hall, a crossing arm and a half-round end. A round building with a ribbed dome stands behind it, and green lawn spreads to the left.",caption:"Technique detail: seen from above, the cathedral is built in the shape of a cross",credit:{word:"Detail photo (from above)",url:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisa_Cathedral_from_Above.jpg",author:"Eric Kilby",license:"CC BY-SA 2.0",licenseUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/",changes:"Resized from the original."}},
 size:"",
 intro:"Work on this Romanesque cathedral in Pisa, Italy, began almost 1,000 years ago. Its builders left almost no wall plain: a few patterns repeat across the cathedral and the bell tower beside it. Why might they have repeated a few patterns instead of designing something new for each wall?",
 context:[{term:"Arcade",pron:"",def:"a row of arches carried on columns or piers. Here, tiers of them climb the front of the cathedral and the tower."},{term:"Romanesque",pron:"roh-muh-NESK",def:"a medieval building style from about 900 to 1200. Thick walls, round arches and sturdy stone piers give it a solid, massive feel, like Roman buildings before it."}],
 clues:[{id:"arches",label:"Tiers of arcades",def:"Rows of small round arches stacked level above level. Trace one tier from side to side. Does it keep the same rhythm all the way across?"},{id:"stripes",label:"Banded marble",def:"Light and dark stone laid in alternating horizontal stripes. Where do the bands run on the cathedral, and where on the tower?"},{id:"diamonds",label:"Diamond-shaped stone panels",def:"Panels of colored stone fitted flush into the marble walls. Where on the building are they set in, and where not?"}],
 steps:["Click a feature box below, then click where you identify the feature on the image. Identify all three features.","Choose any two features to write about. For each, write at least one sentence about your own observations or what you find most interesting."],
 closing:"The walls would stand just as firmly without stripes, diamonds or rows of arches. Why might the builders have added them?",
 bonus:{points:5,prompt:"For 5 bonus points, add any additional observations about the work in general, or question(s) you would like to pursue later.",placeholder:""},
 guide:"Evidence filed. Rows of arches, striped marble and diamond shapes are features a detective can carry to the next case.",
 sourceNums:[79,80,81,82],
 credit:{word:"Photo",url:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_and_Bell_Tower,_Square_of_Miracles,_Pisa_(29409772904).jpg",author:"Ray in Manila",license:"CC BY 2.0",licenseUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/",changes:"Resized from the original."}};
