 intro:"This figure fills a curved wall high above an altar. It is made of thousands of tiny tiles, with gold tiles filling the background. Can you find three features?",
 context:"Pantocrator is a Greek word meaning “ruler of all.” It names a picture of Christ facing the viewer, usually from the chest up.",
 clues:[{id:"gold",label:"Gold background",def:"A flat field of shining gold behind the figure, with no sky or landscape"},{id:"folds",label:"Folds drawn as lines",def:"Cloth shown as bands of straight, parallel lines instead of soft shadows"},{id:"nimbus",label:"Nimbus with a cross",def:"A disk behind the head with a cross set inside it"}],
 steps:["Click a feature box below, then click where you identify the feature on the image. Identify all three features.","Choose any two features to write about. For each, write at least one sentence about your own observations or what you find most interesting."],
 closing:"The makers could have shown a sky, a landscape or a room behind Christ. Why might they have chosen a wall of gold instead?",
