 intro:"In 1305, a painter named Giotto covered the walls of a private chapel in Padua with painted scenes from the life of Christ. In this one, every figure — mourner, rock and angel — bends or dives toward the body of Christ. Why would a painter use even the landscape and the sky to help tell a story about grief?",
 context:[{term:"Lamentation",pron:"",def:"a Christian subject showing the mourning over the body of Christ after he was taken down from the cross."},{term:"Naturalism",pron:"",def:"a style that aims to show people and things as they actually look, instead of in a stiff or formal way."},{term:"Modeling",pron:"",def:"the use of light and shadow in painting or sculpture to make a figure look rounded and solid, as if it has real weight."}],
 clues:[{id:"lean",label:"Mourners leaning in",def:"Figures who bend, kneel and crouch toward the center, so their bodies show their sorrow"},{id:"slope",label:"A slanting rock",def:"A bare hillside that slopes down from the upper right, pointing the eye toward the main figures"},{id:"angels",label:"Angels in the sky",def:"Winged figures that dive through the blue sky, showing grief with their faces and hands"}],
 steps:["Click a feature box below, then click where you identify the feature on the image. Identify all three features.","Choose any two features to write about. For each, write at least one sentence about your own observations or what you find most interesting."],
 closing:"Compare these leaning mourners with the angels on Cimabue’s throne painting. How does each painter show feeling through bodies and poses?",
