var LM24={id:"LM-24",kind:"Architecture",wide:true,title:"Open Arches, a Lacy Walkway and a Patterned Wall",object:"Doge\u2019s Palace, Venice",playable:true,
 crumb:"Late Medieval Period, circa 900 C.E. \u2013 1400 C.E.",
 work:"Doge\u2019s Palace, lagoon front",date:"begun c. 1340 C.E.",location:"Venice, Italy",artist:"Architect unknown",
 headline:"Look closely at the three levels of the wall",
 alt:"A large stone palace seen from below along its waterfront side. At ground level a row of wide pointed arches stands open to the street. Above them runs a second row of slimmer arches on columns, with round carved openings between their tops, forming a covered walkway. Above that rises a solid wall faced in pink and white stone laid in a diamond pattern, with a few tall windows. At the near corner a carved group of two figures stands beneath a small statue. The sky is clear blue.",
 enlarge:"Enlarge image",
 image:"public/images/artworks/Doges-Facade.jpg",
 imageNote:"The view looks up at the south-west corner from the waterfront. Saint Mark\u2019s Basilica stands at the far left.",
 detail:{image:"public/images/artworks/Doges-Corner.jpg",alt:"A close view of the palace's corner. Two carved figures stand on either side of a tree on the angle of the building, with a small winged figure on a pedestal above them. Behind and above rise slim columns with deeply carved leafy capitals, a stone balcony rail, and the pink and white diamond-patterned wall. Wide pointed arches open below.",caption:"Technique detail: the carved corner group of Adam and Eve, with the Archangel Michael above. 14th century.",credit:{"word": "Detail photo (corner)", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venice,_Palazzo_Ducale,_Adam_and_Eve,_Michael.jpg", "author": "Armin Kleiner", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "changes": "Resized from the original."}},
 size:"Work began on the lagoon front in about 1340, under Doge Bartolomeo Gradenigo.",
 intro:"Most big stone buildings put their heaviest walls at the bottom. This one does the opposite. Can you find three features?",
 context:"A loggia (LOJ-ee-uh) is a covered walkway that is open along one side and carried on columns.",
 clues:[{"id": "arches", "label": "Open arches below", "def": "A row of wide pointed arches at ground level, open to the street"}, {"id": "loggia", "label": "Lacy upper walkway", "def": "A second row of slimmer arches on columns, with carved openings between their tops"}, {"id": "pattern", "label": "Patterned wall on top", "def": "A solid upper wall faced in pink and white stone laid in a diamond pattern"}],
 steps:["Click a feature box below, then click where you identify the feature on the image. Identify all three features.", "Choose any two features to write about. For each, write at least one sentence about your own observations or what you find most interesting."],
 closing:"Compare this with Durham and Chartres. Those are churches, built to carry weight downward to the ground. This is a government building, and it puts its heaviest-looking wall on top. What might the builders have wanted people to feel as they walked underneath?",
 bonus:{points:5,prompt:"For 5 bonus points, add any additional observations about the work in general, or question(s) you would like to pursue later.",placeholder:""},
 guide:"Evidence filed. Open arches, a lacy walkway and a patterned wall are features a detective can carry to the next case.",
 sourceNums:[124,125],
 credit:{"word": "Photo", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Doge%27s_Palace_from_Molo,_Venice_-_Venezia_300_77.jpg", "author": "FrDr", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "changes": "Resized from the original."}};
