var LM26={id:"LM-26",kind:"Tomb effigy",wide:true,title:"A Young Face, an Open Book and Long Folds of Cloth",object:"Tomb effigy of Eleanor of Aquitaine",playable:true,
 crumb:"Late Medieval Period, circa 900 C.E. \u2013 1400 C.E.",
 work:"Tomb effigy of Eleanor of Aquitaine",date:"c. 1204 C.E.",location:"Fontevraud Abbey, Anjou, France",artist:"Carver unknown",
 headline:"Look closely at the figure lying on the tomb",
 alt:"Two life-size painted stone figures lie side by side on low tomb chests in a bare stone church. The figure in front is a woman. She lies flat on her back, her head on a pillow at the left and her feet at the right. A white cloth covers her hair, wraps under her chin and frames her face, and a narrow decorated band crosses her forehead. Her face is smooth, oval and young, and her eyes are open. She holds an open book upright in both hands above her chest, as though reading it. A blue cloak lies across her body, and long folds of cream and red cloth run the length of her legs to her feet. The side of the tomb chest beneath her is carved to look like a hanging curtain. Behind her lies a second figure, a man wearing a crown, his eyes closed and his hands resting on his body.",
 enlarge:"Enlarge image",
 image:"public/images/artworks/Fontevraud-Eleanor.jpg",
 imageNote:"Eleanor is in front; her husband Henry II lies behind her. The stone is tuffeau, a pale local limestone. The effigies have been repainted more than once, and the colors visible today may date from a restoration in 1846, so they are not a guide to how the tomb looked in 1204.",
 detail:{image:"public/images/artworks/Fontevraud-Eleanor-Detail.jpg",alt:"A close view of the heads of the same two figures, seen from above. In front, the woman's face is smooth and oval with open eyes and a straight nose, framed by a white cloth that passes under her chin, with a jewelled band across her forehead and worn blue and red paint on the pillow behind her. Her hands hold the open book at the right edge of the view. Behind her, the crowned man lies with his head on a long pillow, his eyes closed. Paint survives in patches on both figures.",caption:"Technique detail: the queen's face and the paint that survives, with Henry II behind her. Photographed in 2025.",credit:{"word": "Detail photo", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Abtei_Fontevraud_-_Grabstelle_(Eleonore_von_Aquitanien).jpg", "author": "Stefan Oemisch", "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "changes": "Resized from the original."}},
 size:"The abbey records that Eleanor commissioned the painted stone effigies for her own tomb and for those of Henry II and Richard the Lionheart before her death in 1204.",
 intro:"This is a portrait of a dead queen, and she is reading. Can you find three features?",
 context:"An effigy (EF-ih-jee) is a carved figure of a dead person, placed on the tomb. One carved lying down is called a recumbent effigy, or a gisant (zhee-ZAHN) in French.",
 clues:[{"id": "face", "label": "A smooth young face", "def": "An oval face with open eyes, calm and unlined, framed by a white cloth that passes under the chin"}, {"id": "book", "label": "An open book", "def": "A book held upright in both hands above her chest, as though she were reading it"}, {"id": "folds", "label": "Long folds of cloth", "def": "Folds of cloak and robe that run the length of the body, following it as it lies flat"}],
 steps:["Click a feature box below, then click where you identify the feature on the image. Identify all three features.", "Choose any two features to write about. For each, write at least one sentence about your own observations or what you find most interesting."],
 closing:"Behind Eleanor lies her husband, Henry II. He is shown in death, hands at rest and eyes closed. She is shown alive and awake, reading. The abbey says Eleanor ordered these figures herself before she died in 1204, which means she chose how she would be seen for the rest of time. Compare her smooth, young face with Uta of Naumburg, then ask yourself: why a book?",
 bonus:{points:5,prompt:"For 5 bonus points, add any additional observations about the work in general, or question(s) you would like to pursue later.",placeholder:""},
 guide:"Evidence filed. A young face, an open book and long folds of cloth are features a detective can carry to the next case.",
 sourceNums:[128,129],
 credit:{"word": "Photo", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gisant_de_l%27Abbaye_de_Fontevraud_DSC_1778.jpg", "author": "GuyFrancis", "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/", "changes": "Resized from the original."}};
