var LM30={id:"LM-30",kind:"Panel painting",title:"A Face Built in Shadow, Heavy Hands and a Working Desk",object:"Saint Jerome, from the Chapel of the Holy Cross",playable:true,
 crumb:"Late Medieval Period, circa 900 C.E. \u2013 1400 C.E.",
 work:"Saint Jerome",date:"c. 1360\u20131365 C.E.",location:"N\u00e1rodn\u00ed galerie, Prague",artist:"Master Theodoric",
 headline:"Look closely at how the man is built",
 alt:"A square painted panel, almost filled by a single man seen from the waist up. He wears a wide red cardinal's hat and a heavy red cloak, and he turns to his right to look down at a book he holds open in both hands. His face is lined and deeply shadowed under the brows and cheekbones, with a short grey curled beard. His hands are large and bony, with raised knuckles and veins, pressed against the green jewelled cover of the book. Behind his shoulder stands a wooden writing desk with a sloping top, a rolled scroll, a dark round inkwell and a long pen. The whole background is gold, pressed into a close diamond pattern that stands up from the surface, and a wide band of the same worked gold runs round the panel as a frame.",
 enlarge:"Enlarge image",
 image:"public/images/artworks/Theodoric-Jerome.jpg",
 imageNote:"Painted for the south window niche of the Chapel of the Holy Cross at Karl\u0161tejn Castle, the room where Emperor Charles IV kept the imperial regalia behind four doors and nineteen locks. The chapel's lower walls are faced with polished jasper and amethyst, and its vault is gilded and set with glass stars. This panel is now in the National Gallery in Prague.",
 detail:{image:"public/images/artworks/Theodoric-Jerome-Detail.jpg",alt:"A second panel of the same set, showing a bishop or pope seen from the waist up, reading a red book held in both hands. He wears a tall white mitre patterned with gold, and a broad band of gold discs down his chest. The point of the mitre rises above the painted field and is carried straight on over the gold frame at the top of the panel. Behind him a writing desk holds books and papers. The background is gold worked in a diamond pattern.",caption:"Technique detail: another panel from the same chapel. The point of the mitre is painted straight on over the gold frame, so the figure seems to push out of its own picture.",credit:{"word": "Detail photo (a second panel)", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Master_Theodoricus_1-IMG_3356.JPG", "author": "PetrDejmek", "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/", "changes": "Resized from the original."}},
 size:"The panel is 114.5 \u00d7 103.7 cm / 45 \u00d7 41 in, painted in oil tempera on beech board. It is one of 129 paintings Master Theodoric made for the chapel.",
 intro:"A man heavy enough to lean on, painted on a flat board. Can you find three features?",
 context:"Modeling is the use of light and shadow to make a flat painting look solid and rounded.",
 clues:[{"id": "face", "label": "A face built in shadow", "def": "Deep shadow under the brows, beside the nose and below the cheekbones, so the head looks solid rather than drawn in outline"}, {"id": "hands", "label": "Heavy hands", "def": "Large bony hands with raised knuckles and veins, pressed against the covers of the book"}, {"id": "desk", "label": "A working desk behind", "def": "A wooden writing desk behind his shoulder, with a rolled scroll, a dark inkwell and a long pen"}],
 steps:["Click a feature box below, then click where you identify the feature on the image. Identify all three features.", "Choose any two features to write about. For each, write at least one sentence about your own observations or what you find most interesting."],
 closing:"Put this face beside the Christ at Ta\u00fcll, painted two hundred years earlier. That one is built from lines: a dark outline with flat color inside. This one is built from shadow, and the outlines have nearly disappeared. The painter, Master Theodoric, was court painter to Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor, and he made one hundred and twenty-nine of these for a single small room. Look at the second panel too: the point of that bishop's mitre does not stop at the edge of the picture \u2014 it is painted straight on over the frame. This is the last case in the file. What has changed between the first case and this one?",
 bonus:{points:5,prompt:"For 5 bonus points, add any additional observations about the work in general, or question(s) you would like to pursue later.",placeholder:""},
 guide:"Evidence filed. A face built in shadow, heavy hands and a working desk are the last features in the Late Medieval file.",
 sourceNums:[136,137],
 credit:{"word": "Photo", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meister_Theoderich_von_Prag_002.jpg", "author": "The Yorck Project", "license": "Public domain", "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/", "changes": "Resized from the original."}};
