 detail:{image:"public/images/artworks/Hunters-Mill.jpg",alt:"Close view of the lower right of the painting. A stone bridge with two arches crosses a frozen pond beside a mill with deep snow on its roofs. A tiny figure carries a bundle of sticks across the bridge. Two women in white caps stand on the ice, joined by a thin line. Dark figures stand on the ice farther back.",caption:"Technique detail: the mill and frozen pond, where tiny figures are painted with just a few careful strokes",credit:{word:"Detail image",url:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pieter_Bruegel_the_Elder_-_Hunters_in_the_Snow_(Detail,_Mill).jpg",author:"Pieter Bruegel the Elder (edited by ZorróAszter)",license:"public domain",licenseUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/",changes:"Resized from the original."}},
 detail2:{image:"public/images/artworks/Hunters-Fire.jpg",alt:"Close view of the lower left of the painting. Outside a brick building, three people work around a small fire on the snow: one leans over a round object on a stand, one reaches into the fire with a long tool, and one bends over holding a bundle of straw. A small child in a dark cap stands at the right. Streaky brushstrokes show in the flames and smoke.",caption:"Technique detail: a close view of the people at work around a fire, where streaky brushstrokes make the flames and smoke",credit:{word:"Detail photo",url:"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hunters_in_the_snow,_1565_-_detail1.jpg",author:"Karmakolle",license:"CC0 1.0",licenseUrl:"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",changes:"Resized from the original."}},
 size:"Height: 117 cm / 46 in. Width: 162 cm / 63.7 in. A little wider than a queen-size mattress.",
 intro:"This winter scene was painted about 460 years ago. Imagine standing on the hilltop beside the hunters. Compare the size of a hunter with the size of a skater on the ice. What do you find as your eye moves from the dark trees to the far mountains? Then look for ordinary people busy at everyday jobs. How many can you find, and where are they?",
 context:"The foreground is the part of a picture nearest to you, and the background is the part farthest away. The middle ground lies between them. Find where each begins in this painting. Which one holds the frozen ponds?",
 clues:[{id:"slope",label:"Tilted ground",def:"A hillside that drops away from the hunters’ feet toward a valley, as if seen from high up"},{id:"shrink",label:"Shrinking figures",def:"People and animals that look large close to you and tiny far away"},{id:"work",label:"Work and play at every distance",def:"Ordinary winter activities, such as tending a fire, carrying wood and skating, shown near, in the middle and far back"}],
